{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnT5ZXkbrcb3exyQtKu9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking whether the overlap between the T-like subspace and the Δq read directions could be inflated, since D_fin weights certain dimensions heavily. To test that, I'm setting up a null baseline using random 5-dimensional subspaces multiplied by dfin and measuring their overlap with v.\n\nI'm checking whether the late-layer Δq read directions aligning with T*dfin (0.23–0.52) could simply be an artifact of dfin concentrating weight on a few dimensions, so I'm building a null baseline from random 5-dimensional subspaces scaled by dfin and comparing their overlap with v. I also need to sort out which \"prediction direction\" is the right one: the residual direction D_fin⊙e versus the writer direction T/D_fin, since the reader at L0–2 and the late read vector live in different spaces.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8853,"cache_read_input_tokens":160848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8853},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9fb2689-71d1-4789-9324-4ca53bd1b486","uuid":"c6a80b15-2fa4-4f43-acab-755188fdf163","timestamp":"2026-11-06T22:18:45.026Z","request_id":"req_011CgnT5ZAfRdCw6bjcsUQhA","thinking_duration_ms":7419,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnT5ZXkbrcb3exyQtKu9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run 24 points somewhere promising, but it needs a control. In the late layers (L11–L17) the top query-change input directions overlap strongly with span(T⊙D_fin): 0.23–0.52, e.g. L15 sv2 0.52, L16 sv0 0.46, L14 sv0 0.44. Their overlap with the plain token subspace T is low, and with T/D_fin it is near 0. T⊙D_fin is the residual direction that most efficiently raises the logit of token t, i.e. a \"the model is predicting t\" representation.\n\nD_fin has a huge dynamic range, though. Any 5-dim subspace multiplied by D_fin concentrates on the few high-D_fin coordinates. If the query deltas also concentrate there for unrelated reasons, the overlap is an artefact. So I'll compare with random 5-dim subspaces scaled by D_fin. If the real overlaps clearly beat this null, the late query changes read the model's current answer prediction. Then a quadratic QK test (predicted token at the query × the same token at the key) gives an absolute sign: copy-confirmation (echo a matching context token) vs copy-suppression. I'll compute that test in the same run, for every late head, with a random-sign null. A positive z means A attends more, from a position predicting t, to context tokens equal to t.\n\n```python\nA = Checkpoint(\"A\"); B = Checkpoint(\"B\")\nP=lambda L:f\"model.layers.{L}.\"\nT=np.load(\"/work/T5mlp.npy\"); dfin=1+A.get(\"model.norm.weight\")\nTf,_=np.linalg.qr(T*dfin[:,None])\nrng=np.random.default_rng(0)\nnul=[]\nVtop={}\nfor L in range(10,18):\n    Di=1+A.get(P(L)+\"input_layernorm.weight\")\n    dq=A.get(P(L)+\"self_attn.q_proj.weight\")-B.get(P(L)+\"self_attn.q_proj.weight\")\n    U,s,Vt=np.linalg.svd(dq,full_matrices=False)\n    Vtop[L]=[(Vt[i]*Di)/np.linalg.norm(Vt[i]*Di) for i in range(3)]\nreal=np.array([[np.linalg.norm(Tf.T@v) for v in Vtop[L]] for L in Vtop])\nfor r in range(200):\n    Q,_=np.linalg.qr(rng.standard_normal((640,5))); Qf,_=np.linalg.qr(Q*dfin[:,None])\n    nul.append([[np.linalg.norm(Qf.T@v) for v in Vtop[L]] for L in Vtop])\nnul=np.array(nul)\nprint(\"real T*dfin overlaps L10-17 (sv0..2):\"); print(real.round(2))\nprint(\"null mean:\"); print(nul.mean(0).round(2)); print(\"null 95%:\"); print(np.quantile(nul,0.95,axis=0).round(2))\nprint(\"empirical p (frac null >= real):\"); print((nul>=real[None]).mean(0).round(3))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8853,"cache_read_input_tokens":160848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8853},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9fb2689-71d1-4789-9324-4ca53bd1b486","uuid":"61de1576-f740-4e88-9a59-8fba8bd010fa","timestamp":"2026-11-06T22:18:52.665Z","request_id":"req_011CgnT5ZAfRdCw6bjcsUQhA"}
